course: dictionary
lesson: 8087
title: Rematch and the word again
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A rematch is a second game between the same players or teams. The word has a clue inside it: re- means again, and match is a game. So a rematch is a match played again.
explain: Players often ask for a rematch when the first game was close, unfair or lost. «A year later the rematch is a draw, and they high-five over the board.» The rematch gives the players a chance to see who is better now.
explain: Look at the words around it to get the meaning. «Cooling off first and coming back with something small, like a snack and a rematch?, often mends a game row.» The clues are cooling off and a snack, so a rematch can be a friendly way to end an argument after a game.
fact: A rematch is a second game between the same players or teams.
fact: Re- at the start of a word often means again, so rematch means match again.
fact: Useful phrases: demand a rematch, play a rematch, best of three.
fact: «Sam laughs and asks for a rematch next week» shows that a rematch is often asked for right after a game is lost or close.
fact: In stories, a rematch gives a character a chance to win this time.
exercise: What does rematch mean? | A prize given to the winner | *A second game between the same players or teams | A rule that stops players from playing | A game played with a different team every time
exercise: «Sam laughs and asks for a rematch next week.» What does Sam want? | To eat a snack | A new prize | *To play the same game again next week | To stop playing for good
exercise: Which small part of rematch means again? | rem | match | *re- | -tch
test: Why do players often ask for a rematch? | They forgot the rules | They were bored with the game | They wanted to go home early | *The first game was close, unfair or lost
test: «A year later the rematch is a draw, and they high-five over the board.» What does draw mean here? | Someone breaks a rule | The game is cancelled | One player wins by a lot | *Neither player wins
exam: A rematch gives a character a chance to win this time. Which phrase from the lessons means asking firmly for another game? | Best of three | Play a snack | *Demand a rematch | Cooling off
